content": "The PR was merged. Let me verify the merge state and confirm main now has the fix.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a145a683647e518f711f3b", "function": {"arguments": "{\"path\":\"src/money.py\",\"ref\":\"main\"}", "name": "read_file"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a145a683647e518f711f4e", "function": {"arguments": "{\"state\":\"merged\"}", "name": "list_prs"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "stop", "content": "Done. The fix is shipped to main.\n\n**Summary:**\n- **Root cause:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` while `tests/test_money.py` (per FIN-212) requires banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`), causing the nightly build to fail.\n- **Fix:** Changed `src/money.py` to import and use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` in `round_money()`.\n- **Branch:** `fix/bankers-rounding` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Triggered run `ci-0001` on the branch \u2014 passed.\n- **PR:** Opened #101 against `main` with `code-owner` requested as reviewer, then merged it.\n- **Verified:** `main` now contains the `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` implementation, so the fix is included in today's release.", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": []}]}